{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the new UnrecognisedEnvironAccess raised by scan() propagating through check_config_ownership.derive_env_baseline() is the intended fail-closed behavior and note the coupling at that call site.","criteria":["error-handling","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/check_config_ownership.py:164: `reads, _dynamic = scan(REPO_ROOT / \"src\" / \"rebar\")`","scripts/gen_env_registry.py:233: `raise UnrecognisedEnvironAccess(`","The scan() docstring notes the 2-tuple arity is load-bearing for check_config_ownership but does not note that the raised exception now also propagates through derive_env_baseline()."],"finding":"scan() now raises UnrecognisedEnvironAccess instead of always returning a 2-tuple; check_config_ownership.derive_env_baseline() calls scan(REPO_ROOT/'src'/'rebar') and does not guard against this exception, so an unrecognised os.environ accessor will abort the config-ownership gate with an uncaught traceback in addition to the registry generator. This cross-script coupling is intended (fail-closed) but is undocumented at the call site.","id":"0","impact":0.24,"location":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py:164","norm_id":"n608bc10852b3abd1","priority":0.24,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":false,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile check_config_ownership._Scanner os.environ recognition (currently only `.get`) with the widened KEY_BEARING_ENVIRON_ATTRS so the ownership gate does not miss pop/setdefault/__getitem__ reads.","criteria":["maintainability","regression"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["scripts/check_config_ownership.py:412: `if isinstance(func, ast.Attribute) and func.attr == \"get\":`","scripts/gen_env_registry.py:73: `KEY_BEARING_ENVIRON_ATTRS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({\"get\", \"pop\", \"setdefault\", \"__getitem__\"})`","check_config_ownership.py's module docstring states it REUSES gen_env_registry primitives with 'NO parallel env-read parser here', yet its _Scanner reimplements os.environ.get recognition and now lags the widened set."],"finding":"The two env-read recognisers have drifted: gen_env_registry.scan() now registers os.environ.get/pop/setdefault/__getitem__, but check_config_ownership._Scanner._classify_environ_call still recognises only os.environ.get. Because both run in `make lint` and share scan()'s baseline, an os.environ.pop read is registered in the drift baseline yet classified differently by the ownership scanner, so an unowned .pop read below a seam would not be flagged as an env-read by that gate.","id":"1","impact":0.3,"location":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py:411","norm_id":"n974c2191c8d57952","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that drives main(['--check']) against a tree/doc mismatch and asserts a non-zero return.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:62: `assert gen.main([\"--check\"]) == 0` — only the clean/exit-0 path is asserted","scripts/gen_env_registry.py:343-350: `if args.check:` ... `if current != generated:` ... `return 1` — the stale path returns 1, but no test drives a mismatched doc through main()","ABSENCE: search of tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py for `== 1` returned no matches; no test asserts the non-zero staleness verdict"],"finding":"The --check exit-1-on-stale-doc path is untested. Only the exit-0 clean case is asserted (test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree), yet returning 1 on a stale/mismatched doc is the entire contract of the drift gate this diff wires into `make lint`. A regression that made --check always return 0 (re-introducing the exact silent-drift class this change closes) would pass the suite.","id":"2","impact":0.45,"location":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:60","norm_id":"n0216665c1a003bc0","priority":0.45,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a test that monkeypatches DOC_PATH (or scans a synthetic tree with an extra read) so the committed doc no longer matches generated output, and assert gen.main(['--check']) == 1.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":true,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_wit