-region","evidence":["scripts/gen_env_registry.py:229-237: `if offenders:` builds `sites = \"\\n\".join(...)` and raises one exception listing every site — explicitly 'report every one at once' per _scan_module docstring (line 188-189)","tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:103: `_scan_source(tmp_path, 'X = os.environ.somenovelaccessor(\"REBAR_FAKE_NOVEL\")\\n')` — exactly one offender site","ABSENCE: no test injects two or more unrecognised accessors and asserts both sites appear in the message"],"finding":"The 'report every offending site at once' contract is untested. scan() collects all offenders across modules and joins them into one UnrecognisedEnvironAccess message, but the only failing-shape test injects a single offender, so a regression that raised on the first offender (or reported only one site) would still pass.","id":"3","impact":0.27,"location":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:98","norm_id":"naf9324d5d4b2399e","novelty":1.0,"priority":0.1929,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Scan a source containing two distinct unrecognised accessors on different lines and assert both attr names and both `:line` markers appear in str(excinfo.value).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allo